# Trivy ignore rules for known acceptable findings.
# Each entry is a Trivy check ID with justification.

# EKS public endpoint enabled — required for CI/CD and developer kubectl access.
# Access is restricted to private CIDRs via public_access_cidrs.
AVD-AWS-0040

# EKS public access CIDRs — restricted to internal ranges, not 0.0.0.0/0.
AVD-AWS-0041

# Security group unrestricted egress — standard pattern for private subnets
# behind NAT gateway. Ingress is restricted.
AVD-AWS-0104

# RDS not using IAM auth — we use Secrets Manager managed credentials.
AVD-AWS-0177

# S3 bucket logging — audit bucket doesn't need access logging on itself.
AVD-AWS-0089

# CloudWatch log group not encrypted — using default AWS encryption.
AVD-AWS-0017

# Public subnets with map_public_ip_on_launch — intentional for ALB/NLB
# ingress and NAT gateway placement. Workloads run in private subnets.
AVD-AWS-0164
